WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.380
When you get hurricanes early like June, July, they don't supposed to be much.

2
00:00:04.380 --> 00:00:07.360
These little tropical storms, but when they get to the island,

3
00:00:07.360 --> 00:00:12.080
I don't know if it's the temperature of the island or the Gulf . . . Hurricane Bill [actually a tropical storm],

4
00:00:12.080 --> 00:00:16.360
Hurricane Danny, Hurricane Cindy was some little tropical depressions.

5
00:00:16.360 --> 00:00:19.900
Well Cindy they finally categorized it as a hurricane the last few years.

6
00:00:19.900 --> 00:00:24.280
But I was stuck for all three storms because they claimed they wasn't going to be much.

7
00:00:24.280 --> 00:00:30.360
They fifty sixty mile an hour winds, but when they get to the island, they get to eighty to 100 miles an hour.

8
00:00:30.360 --> 00:00:34.240
And three hurricanes, little hurricanes . . . Now I wouldn't want to be here for a big one,

9
00:00:34.240 --> 00:00:36.300
but you can see what the little ones do.

10
00:00:36.300 --> 00:00:40.040
It's little storms, but they put a good little punch on you.

11
00:00:40.040 --> 00:00:40.880
It gets you.

12
00:00:40.880 --> 00:00:42.200
It's a wakeup call.

13
00:00:42.200 --> 00:00:49.340
You watch the news, and they always had good weather and all, but they little tropical storms, little depressions, and man,

14
00:00:49.340 --> 00:00:52.680
next thing you know . . . I had my shrimp boat go on land at one time because we didn't leave,

15
00:00:52.680 --> 00:00:55.160
because when a storm comes, we evacuate.

16
00:00:55.160 --> 00:01:00.660
We bring our boats up the bayou by the floodgate; because over here you're going to get over three to four foot of water.

17
00:01:00.660 --> 00:01:04.420
You know, maybe up to six feet of water, and you can't tie your boats like that.

18
00:01:04.420 --> 00:01:07.970
They go up and down, and quite a few boats for Hurricane Danny sunk.
